</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Adieu! ye vain delights of earth;</l><l>Insipid sports, and childish mirth,</l><l>I taste no sweets in you;</l><l>Unknown delights are in the cross,</l><l>All joy beside to me is dross;</l><l>And Jesus thought so too.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>The Cross! O ravishment and bliss—</l><l>How grateful e’en its anguish is;</l><l>Its bitterness how sweet!</l><l>There every sense, and all the mind,</l><l>In all her faculties refined,</l><l>Taste happiness complete.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Self-love no grace in sorrow sees,</l><l>Consults her own peculiar ease:</l><l>’Tis all the bliss she knows;</l><l>But nobler aims true love employ.</l><l>In self-denial is her joy,</l><l>In suffering her repose.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Thy choice and mine shall be the same,</l><l>Inspirer of that holy flame</l><l>Which must forever blaze!</l><l>To take the cross and follow Thee,</l><l>Where love and duty lead, shall be</l><l>My portion and my praise.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
